--- An index outside its array stops the program on the line it is on,
--- with the same words in both modes: inside a function, the function's
--- line (the interpreter named the caller's). A negative index counts from
--- the end, and one past the start stops too (compiled, it printed the
--- index as a huge unsigned number).
fn pick[xs, i]
    return xs[i]
log[pick[[10, 20, 30], -1]]
log[pick[['a', 'b'], 1]]
log[pick[[10, 20, 30], -4]]
log['not reached']
